                "text": "Analyse the transformation rule:\nIn each example, there is a template shape made of 1s and 2s (or blue and red pixels).\nNotice the 2s (red pixels):\nIn the template shape, there are red pixels (2) and blue pixels (1).\nThere are also other isolated/partial red pixels (2) placed elsewhere on the grid.\nThese red pixels serve as \"anchors\" for the template pattern!\nSpecifically, the relative positions of the 2s inside the template determine the orientation/offset, or rather, the template is duplicated/stamped such that its 2s match the positions of the 2s on the board.\n\nLet's check:\nExample 1:\nTemplate:\nRow 0: [1, 2] at cols 5, 6\nRow 1: [1, 1] at cols 5, 6\nRow 2: [2, 1] at cols 5, 6\nRow 3: [0, 1] at col 6\nThe template has two 2s: at (0, 6) and (2, 5).\nDifference between the two 2s: (2 - 0, 5 - 6) = (+2, -1).\nOn the board:\nThere is a 2 at (9, 3) and a 2 at (11, 2).\nNotice: (11 - 9, 2 - 3) = (+2, -1)!\nSo the anchor 2s on the board match the 2s in the template shape!\nWhen the template is stamped there, row 9 col 3 corresponds to (0, 6) -> offset is row 9, col 3 - (0, 6) = (+9, -3).\nThen the shape placed at (+9, -3) covers:\n(0+9, 5-3) = (9, 2): 1\n(0+9, 6-3) = (9, 3): 2\n(1+9, 5-3) = (10, 2): 1\n(1+9, 6-3) = (10, 3): 1\n(2+9, 5-3) = (11, 2): 2\n(2+9, 6-3) = (11, 3): 1\n(3+9, 6-3) = (12, 3): 1\nMatches the output exactly!\n\nExample 2:\nTemplate at rows 3-4:\n(3, 6): 2, (3, 7): 1\n(4, 6): 1, (4, 7): 1, (4, 8): 2\nThe 2s are at (3, 6) and (4, 8).\nRelative vector: (+1, +2).\nOn the board:\nWe have 2s at:\n(7, 9) and (8, 11) -> vector is (8-7, 11-9) = (+1, +2).\n(9, 5) and (10, 7) -> vector is (10-9, 7-5) = (+1, +2).\nSo two copies of the template stamped at those positions!\n\nExample 3:\nTemplate at rows 12-13:\n(12, 3): 2, (12, 4): 1\n(13, 3): 2, (13, 4): 1\nThe 2s are at (12, 3) and (13, 3).\nRelative vector: (+1, 0).\nOther 2s on the board:\n(2, 7) and (3, 7) -> vector (+1, 0)\n(3, 1) and (4, 1) -> vector (+1, 0)\n(14, 10) and (15, 10) -> vector (+1, 0)\nEach pair of 2s is completed to form the template shape!\n\nNow I am ready for the test input. Please provide it.",
